## Model trade-offs

CNN1D had the highest observed mean unseen-home macro-F1 (0.802). GBoost had the lowest mean unseen-home MAE (58.6 W). The table averages appliances equally. Results come from one seeded home split.

| Model | Future-time macro-F1 | Unseen macro-F1 | Unseen MAE (W) | Appliances meeting minimum |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| CNN1D | 0.685 | 0.802 | 63.4 | 3 |
| GBoost | 0.703 | 0.801 | 58.6 | 3 |
| CNN-GRU | 0.683 | 0.798 | 66.0 | 2 |
| MLP | 0.656 | 0.783 | 69.6 | 2 |
| LogReg | 0.616 | 0.729 | 79.5 | 1 |
| Rule | 0.641 | 0.671 | 215.8 | 1 |

## Austin-only versus pooled training

Both fits were scored on the same unseen windows with the pooled training run's physical ON thresholds. Each fit kept its own validation-tuned probability cutoffs. The change reflects both more homes and wider geographic coverage.

| Model | Austin-only macro-F1 | Pooled macro-F1 | Change |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| CNN1D | 0.768 | 0.802 | +0.034 |
| GBoost | 0.783 | 0.801 | +0.018 |
| MLP | 0.744 | 0.783 | +0.039 |

The detailed CSV includes validation, future-time and unseen-home splits, per-region support counts and the four confusion matrix counts. The dashboard shows training curves, confusion matrices and actual versus predicted power.

## Reproduce

```powershell
python -m nilm.experiment --preset multiregion --name multiregion --epochs 5 --max-train 0 --train-per-home 1150 --eval-per-home 600 --regions austin california newyork puertorico --only MLP,CNN1D,Rule,LogReg,GBoost,CNN-GRU
python -m nilm.traces multiregion
streamlit run app.py
```

